    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.sessions\n\n### Description\n\nHello, thank you for the work on mini.nvim\n\n### H.detect_session_local()\nFor a workflow with local sessions in sub-directories from root will not be found by the function, it only checks the cwd but a project might have more depending on the nature (I know global sessions are better but is nice to have an option when required)\n\n### MiniSessions.select()\nAdd a `type` key to `opts` with {'global'|'local'|'all'} and show only corresponding session names in the selector. This would only make sense if there are multiple local sessions tho.",
