    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the suggestion!\n\n> For a workflow with local sessions in sub-directories from root will not be found by the function, it only checks the cwd but a project might have more depending on the nature\n\nThe problem is exactly that there can be more than one session files from sub-directories. There will never be one universally good way to decide which one to use and adding another config for that is a bit too much.\n\nBesides, traversing the whole directory on every startup (to make sure there is no local session in any sub-directory) will have visible impact on the startup time.\n\nSo I think recognizing only local session file in the current working directory is the best approach here.\n\n> Add a `type` key to `opts` with {'global'|'local'|'all'} and show only corresponding session names in the selector. This would only make sense if there are multiple local sessions tho.\n\nLocal session file is always at the top if it is present, which I think is a good trade off without the need for an extra option.",
