        {
            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "Thanks for the fast reply!\n\n> The problem is exactly that there can be more than one session files from sub-directories. There will never be one universally good way to decide which one to use and adding another config for that is a bit too much.\n\nI understand that but the present API provides no way at all, only way is to edit `MiniSessions.detected` which is unreliable. Instead of imposing a single right way, why not provide a flexible and reliable way to help those who want to expand, like a depth key to search how much down the tree for a session file, or take an optional parameter which lists directories to search for (for that particular call)\n```lua\nsessions.select('read', {search = {'sub-dir1', 'sub-dir2'}})\n```\nso the user can accept the overhead (if it exists) or just remove it from their config.\n**There needs to be some way and there is none right now**\n\n> Local session file is always at the top if it is present, which I think is a good trade off without the need for an extra option.\n\nFair",
