        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> Instead of imposing a single right way, why not provide a flexible and reliable way to help those who want to expand ...\n\nBecause this does not align with the main design goal of 'mini.nvim': \"balance between feature-richness (handling as many edge-cases as possible) and simplicity of implementation/support\". The \"local session\" is a more or less established way of saying \"session file in the current working directory\". Anything else is out of scope for 'mini.sessions'.\n\n> **There needs to be some way and there is none right now**\n\nThere is never a **need** for any feature. Only compromises between usefulness and maintenance.",
